<article class="ux-page ux-reading"><header class="ux-page-heading"><p class="ux-eyebrow">Editorial standards</p><h1>Advertising with care.</h1><p>Not every product or service is a fit for this personal platform.</p></header><section class="ux-card"><h2>What we assess</h2><p><?=e(commercial_policy())?></p><p>Evidence may include an official business or product page, actual terms and prices, rights to supplied images, and appropriate credentials for a regulated service. Selecting a category or paying an invoice does not establish that these checks are satisfied.</p></section><section class="ux-card"><h2>Clear separation from independent writing</h2><p>Paid articles and promotional posts identify the sponsor. A paid feature is not an independent product endorsement, and the provider remains responsible for its claims, sales and fulfilment. Sponsored articles do not ask readers to contribute to the writing beneath the feature.</p></section><section class="ux-card"><h2>Approval, scheduling and changes</h2><p>We agree the exact scope and accounts before production. The client reviews factual accuracy and permissions; final editorial approval is separate. Repeat-post automation is limited to the approved, paid campaign and stops for changes or uncertain results. Newsletter advertising, video and ad spend are not silently included.</p></section><section class="ux-card"><h2>Declines and concerns</h2><p>A proposal may be declined or returned for more evidence. Report misleading claims, rights issues or expired information through the contact page. Existing work and any unearned balance are handled according to the agreed service terms; reporting a concern does not itself issue a refund.</p><a href="<?=url('/contact?type=correction')?>">Raise a concern →</a></section><nav class="ux-next-actions"><a href="<?=url('/advertise')?>">Compare the service →</a><a href="<?=url('/promote')?>">Build a suitable brief →</a><a href="<?=url('/editorial-independence')?>">Editorial independence →</a></nav></article>
